WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.950
Dear Minister Vasilev, dear Minister Dimitrov,

2
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.320
dear Mr. Stamenov, Mr. Tsankov, dear Regional Governor,

3
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.830
dear Deputy Mayor,

4
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.070
Your Excellencies, ladies and gentlemen,

5
00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:45.440
Thank you for the great honour of having today's forum under my

6
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:51.120
patronage. I accepted with great pleasure, because I am here in

7
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.199
Varna today to say that the maritime capital of Bulgaria will be a major

8
00:00:56.199 --> 00:01:01.280
technology hub, not only national, not only major in Southeast

9
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.269
Europe, but in the whole of Europe.

10
00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:39.960
Varna has been a city of wide horizons. We think of it as the sea horizon,

11
00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.719
which is boundless. Today this horizon is no longer only maritime,

12
00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:48.230
it is digital, technological and global.

13
00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:53.000
And so the question before us is not whether Europe can, but whether Varna

14
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.709
can be a European technology centre.

15
00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.029
The question is whether we will have that ambition and determination.

16
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.799
And today's forum answers this question categorically.

17
00:02:04.799 --> 00:02:10.710
The answer is yes.

18
00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:46.319
Ladies and gentlemen, all of us in this hall, and our societies, are

19
00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:51.630
convinced that the world is entering a new technological stage.

20
00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:56.239
Not a stage of slow speeds, but of a frantic race,

21
00:02:56.239 --> 00:02:59.390
in which leadership in areas such as artificial intelligence,

22
00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:04.720
semiconductors, quantum technologies and cybersecurity increasingly

23
00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.360
determines the economic and strategic power of every

24
00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.630
society and every country.

25
00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:46.599
Europe must establish its place in this race, it must

26
00:03:46.599 --> 00:03:48.910
have its place and its ambition.

27
00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:53.480
We need more innovation, competitiveness and strategic

28
00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.760
autonomy, which we have recently been talking about a lot.

29
00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.709
Technological sovereignty must be a strategic

30
00:04:01.239 --> 00:04:05.310
priority for Bulgaria too, as a state and part of the European Union.

31
00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.400
Technological sovereignty, ladies and gentlemen,

32
00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.880
does not mean Europe isolating itself from the world, but the opposite:

33
00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.309
it creates, develops and protects the critical technologies

34
00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:44.189
on which its economy and, increasingly, its security depend,

35
00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.710
it has its own knowledge, its own specialists,

36
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.990
well-trained experts, a good education system and, above all,

37
00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.189
the ability to choose its own partners.

38
00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.240
must be a very active part of this process,

39
00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:32.189
and Varna has the potential to become one of its drivers.

40
00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:38.319
Dear friends, the Black Sea is starting to play an ever greater role.

41
00:05:38.319 --> 00:05:42.319
Not only for economic development, not only for the development of

42
00:05:42.319 --> 00:05:43.550
European infrastructure.

43
00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:50.000
The Black Sea is now an indispensable, serious factor for the stability and

44
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.550
security of the whole region and of the whole of Europe.

45
00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:21.520
The wars and conflicts around us made us look differently at

46
00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.039
our Black Sea too,

47
00:06:24.039 --> 00:06:26.710
now also as a strategic security point.

48
00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:31.039
Soon a communication centre will also be built here in Varna, together

49
00:06:31.039 --> 00:06:35.479
with our Romanian colleagues, to transmit information and observations,

50
00:06:35.479 --> 00:06:39.390
which in these very difficult times is of the utmost importance.

51
00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:11.680
Today it is not only fashionable but extremely important to talk about

52
00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:12.990
technological sovereignty.

53
00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:18.919
A moment ago Minister of Innovation Mr. Vasilev spoke in great detail

54
00:07:18.919 --> 00:07:22.479
about the Bulgarian projects, but I cannot fail to note once more

55
00:07:22.479 --> 00:07:26.639
the decision of the European Commission for Bulgaria to be one of the

56
00:07:26.639 --> 00:07:30.520
six countries to build an artificial intelligence gigafactory,

57
00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:35.400
and we have already taken the first steps with the

58
00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.910
BRAIN++ programme, as well as with the company INSAIT.

59
00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:10.000
For centuries, the Black Sea region has been a crossroads of

60
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.110
people, trade and capital.

61
00:08:12.639 --> 00:08:16.149
Today we are adding high technology to this connectivity.

62
00:08:16.759 --> 00:08:20.360
Varna can have its special role as a European technology

63
00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:25.360
centre and as the natural gateway of the European Union to the Black Sea

64
00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:27.270
region and its opportunities.

65
00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:32.200
To be an economic bridge between Bulgaria, the European markets and

66
00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:36.120
the Black Sea region. Thanks to its geographic position,

67
00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.200
port infrastructure, transport links and the development of

68
00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:43.000
the digital economy, the city can connect businesses,

69
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:47.750
capital, technology and human potential from different regions.

70
00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:35.760
Today we are talking about

71
00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.079
high technology, infrastructure projects,

72
00:09:38.079 --> 00:09:42.560
digital projects, but I want to point out to you one

73
00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:48.120
particular emphasis, and that is how technological progress affects

74
00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.990
human life in medicine.

75
00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.120
We must be here, ladies and gentlemen,

76
00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:57.160
especially responsible. I am counting very much in this respect on

77
00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:01.200
your expertise, your experience and your science,

78
00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.680
because when it comes to human health,

79
00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:07.389
technology must be a tool of medical expertise,

80
00:10:08.079 --> 00:10:11.440
and not a substitute. We must develop innovations

81
00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:15.320
that are reliable, transparent and safe, and put the human being at the

82
00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:20.120
centre, because an algorithm can propose the optimal solution,

83
00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:24.720
but cannot by itself bear the moral and professional responsibility

84
00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:25.620
for it.

85
00:11:09.959 --> 00:11:13.480
The European approach to high-risk applications of artificial

86
00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:18.079
intelligence includes requirements for safety, protection of fundamental

87
00:11:18.079 --> 00:11:20.389
rights and human oversight.

88
00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.160
I returned a week ago from the UN General Assembly,

89
00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:28.160
where one of the biggest topics was the future of artificial

90
00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.600
intelligence. In all the round tables, both experts

91
00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:35.440
and politicians agreed that the development of AI

92
00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:39.200
must go in parallel with an analysis of the risks

93
00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:44.120
that this development entails, and the accompanying measures

94
00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:45.550
that must be taken.

95
00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:50.480
Ladies and gentlemen, I saw something very interesting on entering this

96
00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:54.320
hall. Different versions of artificial intelligence,

97
00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:56.430
different machines of the future.

98
00:12:57.199 --> 00:13:00.560
I welcome this forum for the speeches

99
00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:02.800
that will be given, for the debates that will take place here,

100
00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:06.440
for the new proposals, but also for the exhibition itself,

101
00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:09.990
where we can see the achievements of science live.

102
00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:41.749
Let us build technologies that create growth.

103
00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:46.030
Let us build partnerships that create trust.

104
00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:50.480
Let us build infrastructure that creates connectivity and

105
00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:54.199
resilience. And let us build a digital Europe

106
00:13:54.199 --> 00:13:57.110
that is at once innovative, competitive,

107
00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:04.800
secure and free. From Varna to Europe, from the Black Sea to the world and

108
00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:10.279
from ideas to the future. With this I open

109
00:14:10.279 --> 00:14:13.949
today's forum. Good luck and much, much success.

110
00:15:06.839 --> 00:15:09.279
Madam President, it is an honour and a pleasure for us

111
00:15:09.279 --> 00:15:12.720
that you are here. In the corridor, besides technologies of the future,

112
00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:14.629
there were also technologies from the distant past.

113
00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:20.360
The treasure from the Varna Necropolis is in fact the oldest

114
00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:22.160
worked gold in the world.

115
00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:24.509
It is more than 6,000 years old.

116
00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:27.680
And many scholars believe that, besides a symbol of fertility,

117
00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:32.560
the golden bulls actually also hold technologies for

118
00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:36.759
measurements and measures that this civilization should not

119
00:15:36.759 --> 00:15:38.389
have had access to.

120
00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:43.079
So on behalf of the organizers and the partners, we ask you to

121
00:15:43.079 --> 00:15:47.240
accept this as a token of our gratitude for your patronage and

122
00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:50.920
as a technology from the distant past that I hope is still

123
00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.600
relevant in the future.

124
00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:53.880
Thank you for the valuable gift.

125
00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:55.509
Thank you from the heart. Thank you.
